# TTS Text-to-IDs API Server

Converts raw text into integer IDs that your on-device TFLite FastSpeech model expects.

## Setup & Run

```bash
# Install dependencies
pip install -r server_requirements.txt

# Make sure TensorFlowTTS is installed
git clone https://github.com/TensorSpeech/TensorFlowTTS.git
cd TensorFlowTTS && pip install . && cd ..

# Start the server
python api_server.py
```

Server runs at `http://localhost:5000`

## Endpoints

### POST /text2ids
Converts text to integer IDs.

**Request:**
```json
{"text": "Hello, how are you?"}
```

**Response:**
```json
{
  "input_ids": [56, 27, 82, 82, 91, ...],
  "length": 25,
  "text": "Hello, how are you?"
}
```

### GET /health
Returns server status.

## Test It

```bash
# Health check
curl http://localhost:5000/health

# Convert text to IDs
curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/text2ids \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"text": "Hello, how are you?"}'
```

